# Normalise every text file to LF in both the index AND the working tree.
# Removes the fragility of relying on each contributor's core.autocrlf
# setting -- without this, a fresh `git status` on Windows can show
# Makefile / *.c / *.h as modified because the working-tree CRLF
# doesn't match the LF stored in the index. With `eol=lf` the working
# tree is checked out with LF too, so status is deterministic on every
# platform.
#
# Submodule content is NOT covered by this file (third_party/hekate
# manages its own .gitattributes inside the submodule).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
